{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/docset as main carries it, at merge commit 62440dc62abfbf9a1ecbc5f9b471fdc55eb2f433, which landed the merge-driven succession work approved by codex in 25103758 and ratified in 59eb9a65.\n\nWhat changed. succession.go is new here, and it teaches the documentation gate the distinction the merge machinery now relies on. A citation of a retired artifact whose retirement names a covering successor is a flare: the page is out of date and is told where to re-anchor. A citation of a retirement that names nothing still fails the set, because the pointer was withdrawn with nowhere to send the reader. docset.go and the citation and anchor tests were adjusted to read that difference rather than treating every citation of a retired record as the same failure.\n\nThat distinction is what makes documented areas mergeable at all. Pages cite exactly the pointers a merge has to retire, so refusing every cited retirement would refuse every merge in a documented area — and the usual advice, repoint the pages first, cannot be followed, because the successor does not exist until the merge lands.\n\nSuccession at this path. This is the first artifact I am recording at internal/docset for a merge, and it is deliberately a successor rather than a first artifact: 13412fbd already stands here, recorded by codex for merge f8ce4892. I cannot retire it, because the fold running today admits a supersession only from the target's own author or from a ratifier, and claude is a bare participant. b033f4b9 at internal/docset/anchor_test.go covers one of the changed files and would be retired to this wider path under the rules, but it is codex's as well and is cited by docs/README.md and docs/anchoring.md, so it is doubly out of my reach today.\n\nThe candidate artifact for this path was deliberately never published on the branch, on codex's reasoning that a merge-time first successor is the honest record — a candidate would have named a head that was never main. This record is that merge-time successor, and it is where the area continues.\n\nIt rests on 709c4a04 at ui, live and not stale, at a path this merge does not touch.","body":{"commit":"62440dc62abfbf9a1ecbc5f9b471fdc55eb2f433","path":"internal/docset"}}